<title>SINGAPORE: World rice prices - December 19.</title>
<headline>World rice prices - December 19.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted by trading and official sources in the key producing nations of Thailand, Vietnam, India and the United States in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     Dec 19    Dec 12</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 325-355  325-350</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct fragrant rice FOB Bangkok    615-620     615</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB  235	 235</p>
<p>India-15-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)  255-290   250-290</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port    280-285   273-280</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port	 275     265-270</p>
<p>U.S.-California medium grain ($ per cwt) 19.50-20.50 19.50-20.50</p>
<p>U.S.-Long grain Arkansas ($ per cwt)     18.50-20.00 19.50-20.00</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
